            <ArticleTitle>Colloid cyst of the third ventricle and sudden death.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>365-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patients with colloid cysts of the third ventricle may complain only of severe headache. The threat of sudden death makes these patients a special diagnostic problem to the emergency physician. There may be only a few intermittent and nonspecific signs and symptoms associated with this tumor. A discussion of two such cases and an abstract of similar cases drawn from the literature is included in this report.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
